    <string name="onboarding_title">Quiet Answerer</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step1_title">Silence your phone in one tap</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step1_text">Turn on quiet mode for a while: all chosen sound channels go silent and the mode turns itself off later.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step2_title">Automatic SMS replies</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step2_text">Incoming calls are ended and the caller automatically receives a reply SMS with your chosen text.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step3_title">Add the widget</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step3_text">Long-press the home screen, choose the Quiet Answerer widget and drag it onto the home screen to control the mode with one tap.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_start">Get started</string>

    <string name="help_text">How it works:\n\n1. Timer and widget turn the quiet mode on for a chosen time.\n2. All selected sound channels are muted.\n3. Incoming calls are ended (optionally) and the caller receives an auto-reply SMS.\n4. VIP contacts always ring normally.\n5. All events are stored in the Log.\n\nIf the mode can not be silenced because of Do Not Disturb access, the widget shows a faded indicator — grant access in Settings → Sound.</string>
    <string name="about_text">Completely free and open source. No ads, no analytics, no hidden purchases.\n\nAll features are available out of the box.\n\nIcon is derived from the Android robot, distributed under CC BY 3.0.</string>
